\begin{align*}
\gcd(3n+4, n) &= \gcd(n, 3n+4 - 3n)\\
&= \gcd(n, 4)
\end{align*}
Since $n$ can be any positive integer, the possible values of $\gcd(n, 4)$ are 1, 2, and 4. To find the sum of all possible values, we simply add these numbers together:
\begin{align*}
1 + 2 + 4 &= 7
\end{align*}
